    "available_at": "2026-11-04T18:02:51.666626+00:00",
    "body": "Canaccord Genuity senior investment advisor Cam Currie.\nPosted By: Adrian Pocobelli November 4, 2026\nThis week’s episode features Cam Currie , Senior Investment Advisor at Canaccord Genuity Wealth Management and leader of the Currie Metals & Mining Group, in conversation with host Adrian Pocobelli about the outlook for precious metals and mining stocks.\nCurrie explains why mining equities are beginning to look attractive again following the recent pullback in gold below US$4,000 per ounce and silver below US$50 per ounce. He also discusses why the long-term fundamentals for precious metals remain strong, particularly against a backdrop of rising sovereign debt across Western economies. Currie also shares his outlook for copper and other critical minerals stocks.\nThis week’s Spotlight features Adrian O’Brien , Vice President of Business Development and Communications at Midnight Sun Mining, who provides an update on the company’s copper project in Zambia. To learn more, visit https://midnightsunmining.com/ .\nThe Northern Miner · Canaccord Genuity’s Cam Currie talks precious metals stocks\n“Rattlesnake Railroad”, “Big Western Sky”, “Western Adventure” and “Battle on the Western Frontier” by Brett Van Donsel ( ⁠www.incompetech.com⁠ ).\nLicensed under Creative Commons: By Attribution 4.0 License\n⁠creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0⁠\nApple Podcasts: ⁠ https://podcasts.apple.com/ca/podcast/the-northern-miner-podcast/id1099281201⁠\nSpotify: ⁠ https://open.spotify.com/show/78lyjMTRlRwZxQwz2fwQ4K⁠\nYouTube: ⁠ https://www.youtube.com/@NorthernMiner⁠\nSoundcloud: ⁠ https://soundcloud.com/northern-miner Print\nTAG: Podcast\nCOMMODITY: Gold Silver\nRepublish this article",
